  "body": "Just ported another test file to wpt. There is one thing where I'm unsure if this is the correct way for assertion. In some tests the constructor of the error object is compared. I couldn't get it to work without casting it to a string first.\n\nFor example:\n\n``` js\nconst ws = new WritableStream();\nconst writer = ws.getWriter();\nwriter.write().then(\n   () => { throw new Error('something failed'); },\n   r => assert_equals(r.constructor.toString(), TypeError.toString(), 'err message')\n);\n```\n",
